.TH OROC-UPDATE-SIGN 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.1.4" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-update\-sign \- Sign an update manifest and emit a detached manifest.sig file.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc update sign [\-\-manifest=<path>] (\-\-keys=<file> | \-\-private\-key=<hex>) [options]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Sign an update manifest and emit a detached manifest.sig file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-manifest=<path>\fR
path to the manifest JSON file to sign (default: manifest\-name or ORO_UPDATE_MANIFEST_FILENAME)
.TP
\fB\-\-manifest\-name=<name>\fR
manifest filename to use when \-\-manifest is not provided
.TP
\fB\-\-keys=<file>\fR
JSON file containing a signing key (with "privateKey" or "secretKey" field)
.TP
\fB\-\-private\-key=<hex>\fR
Ed25519 private key as a hex string
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-id=<id>\fR
optional key identifier to embed in manifest.sig (default: "pk\-1")
.TP
\fB\-\-out=<path>\fR
output path for manifest.sig (default: <manifest\-without\-extension>.sig, e.g. manifest.json \-> manifest.sig)
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file=<path>\fR
mirror logs to a JSON file
.SH NOTES
.PP
The signature file is JSON containing "schemaVersion", "algorithm", "keyId", and "signature" fields. Clients verify manifest bytes against manifest.sig and the configured public key(s). Advanced: set ORO_UPDATE_MANIFEST_FILENAME or pass '\-\-manifest\-name' to change the default manifest filename.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBoroc update sign \-\-keys key.json \-\-manifest manifest.json\fR
sign manifest.json using the private key in key.json
.TP
\fBoroc update sign \-\-private\-key <hex\-private\-key> \-\-manifest manifest.json \-\-out manifest.sig\fR
sign a manifest using a raw hex private key
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1), oroc\-update(1)
